Home responsive behavior

Alva is designed for desktop and landscape mobile/tablet play, so the new Home needs to remain strong at short viewport heights.

Do not simply hide the entire road at smaller widths the way the old fighter preview is currently hidden.

Instead, adapt it.

On smaller/narrower layouts, allow the road to move farther off the right edge and behave more like a decorative background strip.

Keep the large ALVA title readable and prevent it from colliding with Play/Help controls.

At very short landscape heights, reduce vertical gaps, kicker spacing, title scale, and button height before removing meaningful content.

The green separator should remain visible whenever practical.

Do not introduce scrolling on the main Home screen.

Respect safe-area insets.

Motion

The Home entrance animation can retain Alva’s existing fade/rise character, but adapt it to the new elements.

The road lane motion can run continuously at low intensity.

A slow translation such as Seren’s approximately 1.4-second repeating lane cycle is a reasonable reference.

The green slash itself should remain mostly stable. If it animates on entrance, use a short smooth reveal rather than perpetual pulsing.

Respect:

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)

When reduced motion is requested, lane scrolling and decorative entrance motion should stop or effectively become instantaneous.

Do not interfere with the existing ScreenManager transitions.

