Implementation quality

Keep the implementation concise and consistent with the existing codebase.

Prefer changing shared semantic color variables over duplicating literal colors across dozens of selectors.

Where current variable semantics conflict with the new theme, introduce appropriately named semantic variables instead of forcing an old variable to mean two contradictory things.

Keep Home-specific styling under the existing Home section of styles.css.

Keep non-Home changes limited to theme/color corrections.

Avoid !important unless genuinely required by an existing specificity conflict.

Avoid visual effects that do not exist elsewhere in the design system.

No excessive gradients, glassmorphism, glow, rounded cards, or animated decoration.

The result should feel like Alva redesigned by the same visual system that produced Seren, not like Seren copied directly into Alva.

